- content_for :title, "Garages"
.garages{style: "max-width: 900px;"}
  %h2
    Garages
    - if can?(:edit, Vehicle)
      = link_to "Add a garage", new_garage_path, class: "btn btn-primary btn-sm pull-right"
  %p.text-muted
    The yards this agency's buses live at. A bus's runs start and end at its garage, so moving a bus is a pick from this list on the bus's page; fixing a garage here fixes it for every bus and run that uses it.
  %p.text-muted
    Buses whose runs start far from their garage, and runs still starting at a yard their bus has left, are listed on the
    = succeed "," do
      = link_to "Address check", address_checks_path
    checked each morning.
  - if @garages.empty?
    %p{style: "color: #0ca30c;"} Garages you add show up here, and in the Garage list on each bus.
  - else
    %table.table.table-condensed
      %thead
        %tr
          %th Garage
          %th Address
          %th{style: "text-align: right;"} Buses
          %th
      %tbody
        - @garages.each do |g|
          %tr{style: (g.inactive ? "color: #5f6b7a;" : "")}
            %td
              %b= g.name
              - if g.inactive
                %span.label.label-default Retired
            %td= [g.address, g.city, g.zip].compact.join(", ")
            %td{style: "text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;"}= @counts[g.id].to_i
            %td{style: "text-align: right; white-space: nowrap;"}
              - if can?(:edit, Vehicle) && !g.inactive
                = link_to "Edit", edit_garage_path(g)
                &nbsp;
                = link_to "Retire", retire_garage_path(g), method: :patch, data: { confirm: "Retire #{g.name}? It can't be while a bus or an upcoming run uses it." }
